{
  "_readme": [
    "The deterministic fit scorer's inputs. Copy this file to fit_profile.json",
    "and edit that copy - fit_profile.json is gitignored because it encodes who",
    "you are, while this example is tracked and carries no real profile.",
    "",
    "Every number here is a tunable. The five component maxima in weights.max",
    "must sum to 100; the scorer refuses to load a profile where they do not.",
    "",
    "Two rules the values encode, worth keeping in mind when editing:",
    "  P1 - a missing skill is not a missing qualification. The skills block",
    "       only ever ADDS, and saturates fast. Only skills.exclude counts",
    "       against a posting, and it gates rather than deducts.",
    "  P2 - preference is a first-class signal. roles and company affinity are",
    "       42 of 100 on purpose. This is a reading-order prior, not a",
    "       capability assessment."
  ],
  "version": 1,

  "roles": {
    "_comment": [
      "Graded by how much you want that kind of role. Title evidence has strict",
      "precedence: if the title names any family, the description cannot",
      "override it - so a Data Scientist posting full of AI wording stays a",
      "Data Scientist. Terms must be phrase-specific; a bare 'engineer',",
      "'research', 'data', 'ai' or 'platform' must never assign a family."
    ],
    "description_factor": 0.6,
    "cap_families": ["adjacent"],
    "families": {
      "ai_engineer": {
        "score": 25,
        "terms": ["ai engineer", "a.i. engineer", "ai engineering", "ai/ml engineer",
                  "ai and ml engineer", "ai/ml", "ai developer",
                  "artificial intelligence engineer", "artificial intelligence developer",
                  "applied ai", "applied ai engineer",
                  "llm", "llms", "large language model", "large language models",
                  "llm engineer", "llm systems engineer", "llm infrastructure",
                  "nlp", "nlp engineer", "nlp scientist", "natural language processing",
                  "agentic ai", "agentic", "generative ai", "gen ai", "genai",
                  "conversational ai", "ai software engineer", "ai platform engineer",
                  "research engineer", "ai research engineer", "prompt engineer",
                  "rag engineer", "retrieval augmented generation"]
      },
      "software_engineer": {
        "score": 22,
        "terms": ["software engineer", "software developer", "software engineering",
                  "software dev engineer", "software development engineer",
                  "backend engineer", "back-end engineer", "backend developer",
                  "back end developer", "full stack engineer", "fullstack engineer",
                  "full-stack engineer", "full stack developer", "fullstack developer",
                  "full-stack developer", "platform engineer", "python developer",
                  "typescript developer", "web developer", "application engineer",
                  "swe", "sde"]
      },
      "ml_engineer": {
        "score": 16,
        "terms": ["machine learning", "machine learning engineer", "ml engineer",
                  "mlops engineer", "mlops", "ml ops", "ml platform engineer",
                  "ml infrastructure engineer", "machine learning infrastructure",
                  "machine learning operations", "machine learning developer",
                  "ml developer", "deep learning", "deep learning engineer",
                  "deep learning developer", "computer vision", "computer vision engineer"]
      },
      "data_scientist": {
        "score": 12,
        "terms": ["data scientist", "research scientist", "applied scientist",
                  "data engineer", "machine learning scientist", "quantitative researcher",
                  "analytics engineer", "decision scientist"]
      },
      "generic_engineering": {
        "_comment": [
          "The catch-all for a title that is plainly an engineering job but names",
          "no family: 'Compiler Engineer', 'Rust Engineer', 'Backend-Entwickler'.",
          "Without it the role floor treats those exactly like 'Sales Manager' and",
          "forces them to Low, which is far too blunt - they are real targets, just",
          "not obviously the kind you are hunting. Scoring 14 keeps them below every",
          "named family while leaving the floor for postings that are genuinely not",
          "engineering at all."
        ],
        "score": 14,
        "terms": ["engineer", "developer", "entwickler", "programmer", "programmierer",
                  "engineering", "softwareentwickler"]
      },
      "adjacent": {
        "score": 5,
        "terms": ["solutions engineer", "solution engineer", "forward deployed engineer",
                  "forward-deployed engineer", "sales engineer", "data analyst",
                  "developer advocate", "developer relations", "technical account manager",
                  "product manager", "business analyst", "support engineer",
                  "consultant", "consulting", "berater", "presales", "pre-sales",
                  "customer success", "trainer", "evangelist", "recruiter"]
      }
    }
  },

  "seniority": {
    "_comment": [
      "The sharpest discriminator for a new graduate, and the one place the",
      "scorer reads the title and the body by different rules. The full ladder",
      "is read from the TITLE only - 'Senior' in a job title is unambiguous.",
      "From the BODY only the years-of-experience regex and explicit entry",
      "markers count, because 'reporting to the Head of AI' and 'you will work",
      "with senior engineers' are not seniority requirements. When both fire,",
      "the lower score wins."
    ],
    "scores": {
      "entry": 25,
      "none": 20,
      "one_two": 17,
      "three_plus": 8,
      "senior": 3,
      "lead": 0
    },
    "years_bands": [
      {"max_years": 0, "level": "entry"},
      {"max_years": 2, "level": "one_two"},
      {"max_years": 3, "level": "three_plus"},
      {"max_years": 6, "level": "senior"},
      {"max_years": 99, "level": "lead"}
    ],
    "entry": ["graduate", "new grad", "new graduate", "junior", "entry level",
              "entry-level", "intern", "internship", "working student", "werkstudent",
              "trainee", "praktikum", "absolvent", "berufseinsteiger", "no experience required"],
    "one_two": [],
    "three_plus": ["mid-level", "mid level", "midlevel"],
    "senior": ["senior", "sr.", "experienced professional", "erfahrene"],
    "lead": ["lead", "team lead", "tech lead", "technical lead", "staff engineer",
             "principal", "head of", "manager", "director", "architect",
             "vice president", "engineering manager", "chief"],
    "experience_markers": ["experience", "experienced", "erfahrung", "berufserfahrung",
                           "background", "hands-on", "hands on", "practical", "working",
                           "track record", "praxis"],
    "marker_window": 60
  },

  "skills": {
    "_comment": [
      "Additive only. A posting that names nothing you know scores 0 here; it is",
      "never penalised, because a skill you have not used is usually a",
      "vocabulary gap rather than a capability gap (P1). Saturation is the",
      "weight-point total that earns full marks - low on purpose.",
      "Bare 'ai' and 'ml' belong in roles, never here: they are far too common",
      "in prose to carry a weight of 3.",
      "exclude is the one negative list: stacks you have decided not to pursue.",
      "It GATES (band -> low) rather than deducting, and only when the stack is",
      "the role's primary one - named in the title, or inside a must-have line."
    ],
    "saturation": 10,
    "primary": ["python", "pytorch", "transformers", "hugging face", "huggingface",
                "nlp", "natural language processing", "llm", "llms", "large language model",
                "large language models", "rag", "retrieval augmented generation",
                "retrieval-augmented generation", "typescript", "fastapi", "react",
                "next.js", "nextjs", "sql"],
    "secondary": ["docker", "aws", "postgresql", "postgres", "langchain", "langgraph",
                  "embeddings", "embedding", "vector database", "vector search", "pgvector",
                  "spacy", "scikit-learn", "sklearn", "java", "spring boot", "django",
                  "kubernetes", "sentence-transformers", "bertopic", "chromadb", "supabase"],
    "domain": ["agentic", "evaluation", "forecasting", "topic modelling", "topic modeling",
               "github actions", "nginx", "redis", "slurm", "hpc", "retrieval",
               "ci/cd", "terraform", "prometheus", "grafana", "caddy", "stripe"],
    "exclude": [".net", "dotnet", "asp.net", "c#", "php", "sap abap", "abap", "cobol",
                "delphi", "vb.net", "visual basic", "sharepoint", "salesforce apex"],
    "must_have_markers": ["required", "requirements", "must have", "must-have", "essential",
                          "you have", "we expect", "vorausgesetzt", "erforderlich",
                          "zwingend", "your profile", "qualifications"],
    "exclude_counter_markers": ["migration", "migrating", "migrate", "legacy", "replace",
                                "replacing", "modernis", "moderniz", "interoperab",
                                "integration with", "phase out", "sunset", "away from"]
  },

  "geo": {
    "_comment": [
      "EDIT THESE FIRST. `home`, `belt`, `second` and `third` are placeholders",
      "for wherever you actually want to work - the real ordering lives in your",
      "private fit_profile.json, not here. The country and region lists below",
      "are plain geography and can stay as they are.",
      "",
      "Keep the top tiers close together: they express a preference between",
      "places you would all accept, not a gap in suitability. An unresolved",
      "location scores NEUTRAL, never zero - an unknown is not a negative, and",
      "zeroing it would bury every board that omits the field. No visa, permit",
      "or relocation signal appears anywhere here, by design: those are never",
      "grounds to discount a posting.",
      "Buckets are tested in the order listed under `order`, most specific first."
    ],
    "scores": {
      "home": 15, "belt": 14, "second": 14, "third": 13,
      "ch_other": 10, "de_at": 9, "eu": 8, "unknown": 8, "outside": 0
    },
    "order": ["home", "belt", "second", "third", "ch_other", "de_at", "eu", "outside"],
    "home": ["your-home-city"],
    "belt": ["a-town-you-would-commute-to", "another-commutable-town"],
    "second": ["your-second-choice-city"],
    "third": ["your-third-choice-city"],
    "ch_other": ["switzerland", "schweiz", "suisse", "svizzera", "basel", "bern", "berne",
                 "geneva", "genève", "genf", "lausanne", "st. gallen", "st gallen",
                 "sankt gallen", "lugano", "neuchâtel", "neuchatel", "fribourg", "sion",
                 "chur", "biel", "bienne", "thun", "solothurn", "olten", "zurich area"],
    "de_at": ["germany", "deutschland", "austria", "österreich", "oesterreich",
              "hamburg", "frankfurt", "cologne", "köln", "koeln", "stuttgart",
              "düsseldorf", "dusseldorf", "duesseldorf", "leipzig", "dresden",
              "nuremberg", "nürnberg", "nuernberg", "hannover", "bremen", "essen",
              "dortmund", "karlsruhe", "mannheim", "bonn", "münster", "augsburg",
              "heidelberg", "darmstadt", "ulm", "freiburg", "potsdam", "jena",
              "vienna", "wien", "graz", "linz", "salzburg", "innsbruck"],
    "eu": ["europe", "european", "emea", "netherlands", "amsterdam", "utrecht",
           "france", "paris", "lyon", "spain", "madrid", "barcelona", "italy", "milan",
           "rome", "turin", "portugal", "lisbon", "porto", "poland", "warsaw", "krakow",
           "czech", "prague", "sweden", "stockholm", "denmark", "copenhagen", "norway",
           "oslo", "finland", "helsinki", "ireland", "dublin", "belgium", "brussels",
           "luxembourg", "united kingdom", "london", "cambridge", "oxford", "manchester",
           "edinburgh", "romania", "bucharest", "hungary", "budapest", "estonia",
           "tallinn", "greece", "athens", "bulgaria", "sofia", "croatia", "zagreb"],
    "outside": ["united states", "usa", "u.s.", "new york", "san francisco", "california",
                "seattle", "boston", "austin", "chicago", "denver", "canada", "toronto",
                "vancouver", "india", "bangalore", "bengaluru", "hyderabad", "singapore",
                "japan", "tokyo", "china", "shanghai", "beijing", "shenzhen", "hong kong",
                "australia", "sydney", "melbourne", "israel", "tel aviv", "dubai",
                "abu dhabi", "brazil", "sao paulo", "são paulo", "mexico", "argentina",
                "south africa", "cape town", "new zealand", "seoul", "taipei"]
  },

  "company": {
    "_comment": [
      "Affinity 0-5 lives in company_affinity.json. Resolution order is",
      "explicit: your rating wins; failing that an ATS registry tier seeds it;",
      "only a company with neither falls back to `default`. So 'unrated' does",
      "not mean one fixed score - a tier-1 company with no rating seeds to 4."
    ],
    "tier_seed": {"1": 4, "2": 3, "3": 2, "4": 1, "5": 1},
    "match_threshold": 85
  },

  "weights": {
    "_comment": [
      "max must sum to 100. bands are the display thresholds; calibrate them",
      "against a hand-labelled set rather than a histogram - a histogram shows",
      "the distribution, not whether the top of the list is right."
    ],
    "max": {"role": 25, "seniority": 25, "skills": 18, "company": 17, "location": 15},
    "bands": {"high": 75, "medium": 58}
  }
}
